{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7ac2c7ec9e5841f462fd548b2adbe08c1ec463d3900447ddd03e9345d1fe8c94","digest":{"component_or_area":"snapshot janitor / disk reclaim","key_entities":["src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py","DEFAULT_FREE_WATERMARK_BYTES","free_watermark_pct","RECLAIM_TARGET_MARGIN_PCT","run_gc()","_gc_pass()","src/rebar/_config_sources.py","REBAR_GATE_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py","materialize_tickets","repo_snapshot.py","store_root()"],"problem_keywords":["disk pressure","garbage collection","reclaim","watermark","snapshot store","root volume","volume-relative threshold"],"propositions":["The snapshot janitor's 2 GiB absolute free-space watermark is unreachable on a 30 GiB volume (only crossed at 93.3% used, above the 85% alarm floor and 90% incident peak), so reclaim never engages before the alarm fires.","Every review materializes a full ~620 MiB copy of the ticket tree keyed on a tip advancing every ~26 seconds with minimal reuse, causing ~4.4 GiB/hour root-disk growth that reclaim cannot service.","The store is placed on the root volume's ephemeral writable layer because REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR is unset everywhere, making it invisible to docker prune and freed only on container recreation.","The janitor requires a volume-relative reclaim trigger that scales the threshold below the alarm floor on small volumes, with hysteresis to prevent re-firing at every interval."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787709890301680001,"uuid":"d82e4298-b8a5-4dd1-8475-b38f94d9ab98"}